desktop-shell-window-context-menu(1)

# NAME

desktop-shell-window-context-menu - menu for a window, opened by right-clicking its title bar

# SYNOPSIS

*desktop-shell-window-context-menu* [*-c* _FILE_] [*-s* _FILE_]

# DESCRIPTION

*desktop-shell-window-context-menu* shows a menu for a window: its title,
application, process ID and memory, then Close, End process (SIGTERM), Force
close (SIGKILL), Pause and Resume process, copying the process ID, title,
application name, command line or working directory, and Floating,
Fullscreen, Sticky, Move to workspace and Move to scratchpad.

It opens when sway runs a binding that marks the window and names the
program, as the installed configuration does for right-clicks on title bars:

```
bindsym button3 mark --add _window-context-menu-target, nop desktop-shell-window-context-menu
```

Mouse bindings act on the window under the pointer; key bindings act on the
focused window. The menu opens at the pointer. Process actions are disabled
for X11 windows, whose process ID belongs to the X server, and signals use a
pidfd taken when the menu opens, so they never reach a process that reused
the ID. After a package upgrade, *swaymsg reload* restarts the program from
the new file.

# OPTIONS

*-h, --help*
	Show the help message and exit.

*-c, --config* _FILE_
	Read settings from _FILE_ instead of the usual places.

*-s, --style* _FILE_
	Load _FILE_ instead of the shipped window-context-menu.css.

# CONFIGURATION

The installed _@sysconfdir@/sway/config.d/60-desktop-shell-window-context-menu.conf_
starts the program and adds the right-click binding.

# SETTINGS

Read from _$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/desktop-shell-components/window-context-menu.ini_,
else _/etc/xdg/desktop-shell-components/window-context-menu.ini_. All are
optional; *swaymsg reload* applies changes.

*[menu]*
	*enabled* = _true_|_false_

*[appearance]*
	*follow-sway-bar* = _true_|_false_

# STYLING

The menu is a popover with the _window-context-menu_ class, styled in
_shared-theme.css_ with the theme's color variables.

# SEE ALSO

*sway*(5), *desktop-shell-workspace-window-bar*(1)
